Package: postrank
Type: Package
Title: Posterior Ranking with Integer Grades
Version: 1.3.0
Authors@R:
    person("JoonHo", "Lee", email = "jlee296@ua.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0006-4019-8703"))
Description: Assigns integer grades to entities from posterior draws, analytic
    normal or mixture distributions, or precomputed pairwise comparison
    probabilities on one or several criteria. Minimizes posterior expected
    wrong-direction errors plus a cost per pair left unordered in the same
    grade, producing one common grading across criteria or separate per-domain
    grades with joint error-exceedance caps ('gmp'). Model fitting takes place
    outside the package. Supports per-criterion error budgets, worst-criterion
    (minimax) loss, exact grade counts, and a separate loss mode for posteriors
    with exact ties. Uses 'Gurobi' by default or 'HiGHS' when selected, while
    stored examples, tables, 'ggplot2' figures, HTML reports, and Monte Carlo
    or IID diagnostics run without a solver. Builds on the report-card
    framework of Kline, Rose, and Walters (2024) <doi:10.1257/aer.20230700>.
